    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12190" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cypărissa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ia</span></b> ), ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town in Messenia</i>, now <i>Arkadhia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 5,
				7, § 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
			21</span></i>; called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cypărissae</span></b> ,
			ārum, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
			9</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cypărissĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to Cyparissa</i>: sinus, <i>Gulf of
				Arkadhia</i>, Plin. l. l.; Mel. l. l.</div>
